  "known_limitations": [
    "The procedural RGB degradations are controlled evaluation proxies, not exact simulations of material aging, moisture transport, pigment chemistry, varnish change, or conservation treatment.",
    "Only 50 of 165 generated cases have an approved localized inpainting objective; excluded cases must not be treated as model failures.",
    "Five paintings are the independent units; 50 cases and 150 core candidates are repeated observations nested within those paintings.",
    "One painting per category means painting and category effects cannot be separated.",
    "Configured severity is ordinal and is not a calibrated conservation-condition grade.",
    "Affected area is partly determined by degradation family and severity, so associations are descriptive rather than independent causal effects.",
    "The water-stain-dirt comparison is an ordered computational composition and cannot establish physical interaction or synergy.",
    "Stable Diffusion uses one preselected primary candidate per case; prompt-context candidates are outside this comparison.",
    "The six-case SDXL subset is incomplete, severity-imbalanced, and descriptive only.",
    "No synthetic-degradation repeated-seed population exists in Notebooks 18 or 19; this notebook does not estimate generative uncertainty.",
    "General-purpose image metrics are computational proxies rather than human, historical, or conservation judgements.",
